Technical feasibility review for epic {{.id}}: "{{.title}}".

LOAD: architecture skill workflows (design-system, design-backend, design-frontend, design-database, design-security) as applicable. LOAD: specification-writing workflow plan/epic-tech-plan.md.

PLAN GATE — run before creating any document:
(1) READ: shark epic context get {{.id}} --json
(2) IF context_data.tech_remaining_steps non-empty: RESUME MODE — skip to ACT with tech_remaining_steps.
    Log: shark epic note {{.id}} 'Resuming tech feasibility review. Remaining: [...]. Completed: [...].'
(3) IF context_data.tech_remaining_steps empty: PLAN MODE — run epic-tech-plan.md decision tree.
    For each optional tech doc: state INCLUDE or EXCLUDE with specific reason for THIS epic.
    Default to INCLUDE when uncertain.
    Store: shark epic context set {{.id}} --field tech_remaining_steps '[...]'
           shark epic context set {{.id}} --field tech_implementation_decisions '{...}'
           shark epic context set {{.id}} --field tech_plan_created_at 'TIMESTAMP'
    Log: shark epic note {{.id}} 'TECH PLAN: Will create N docs: [list]. Excluded: [...].' --type=decision

READ:
(1) All epic BA docs (just validated by BA check) — use shark related-docs list --epic={{.id}}
(2) Research report from the research phase
(3) BA feasibility review report
(4) Other epic architectures and PRDs under docs/plan/ for system-wide awareness

EVALUATE:
(1) Technical feasibility -- can each requirement area be implemented with available technology and team capabilities?
(2) Architectural concerns -- does research reveal integration complexity, performance risks, or scaling issues?
(3) Dependency and integration risks -- are there external system dependencies or cross-epic technical conflicts?
(4) Technical debt implications -- will this epic create or exacerbate technical debt?

ACT: Create only documents in tech_remaining_steps.
     Follow patterns from research — do not reinvent existing patterns.
     After each doc: update tech_completed_steps.

PRODUCE: Technical feasibility review report with findings for each area, overall assessment (APPROVED or CONCERNS_FOUND), and recommended actions.

IF APPROVED: Advance via shark epic update {{.id}} --status=ready_for_tech_check.

IF CONCERNS FOUND: Set intervention_required via shark epic update {{.id}} --status=intervention_required, and write a structured intervention report detailing what's wrong, options, and recommended action.
